&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; As of current, SCP-5958 does not need to be contained. All SCP-5958 resources are to be focused on successful reenactment of SCP-5958-B.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prior Containment Procedures (Last Effective 12/31/2020):&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5958 is to be kept in Site-411&#039;s Cognitohazardous Ward in a windowless cell. Food is to be delivered by Class-D personnel at a routine schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under no circumstances are Foundation personnel to interact with SCP-5958. Should any Foundation personnel attempt to interact with SCP-5958 in any capacity, they are to be terminated without warning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5958 referred to a cognitohazardous entity by the name of Elias Cardinal that was in Foundation containment from April 7th, 2020 until January 1st, 2021. SCP-5958&#039;s cognitohazardous abilities were capable of changing one&#039;s memories.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5958&#039;s initial containment squad and Class-D personnel who interacted with SCP-5958 showed an express interest in arguing for SCP-5958, as well as behaviors not commonly associated with them prior to exposure to SCP-5958. As of current, only amnestic treatment seems to remove this effect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery:&lt;/strong&gt; On April 6th, 2020, SCP-5958 was found to be using its cognitohazardous abilities to amnesticize witnesses to assorted crimes&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-136059-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Foundation personnel acting as civilian authorities apprehended SCP-5958 later that night, before bringing SCP-5958 into Foundation containment at 1:29AM EST the following morning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explanation Report:&lt;/strong&gt; On January 1st, 2020, as part of Foundation-mandated containment checks&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-136059-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, SCP-5958 was interviewed by Senior Researcher Thatcher.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Researcher Thatcher concluded the interview with the belief that SCP-5958&#039;s cognitohazardous abilities were not exclusive to SCP-5958 themselves, but rather to a kinetoglyph&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-136059-3&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; that SCP-5958 performed. Senior Researcher Thatcher claims that SCP-5958 demonstrated the kinetoglyph, but all attempts to recreate the effects have failed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This kinetoglyph has been deemed SCP-5958-B. SCP-5958 itself has been deemed explained.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-136059-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Including petty theft, breaking and entering, assault and battery, robbery, and various degrees of murder.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-136059-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. Annual process of examining all SCP objects in the Foundation&#039;s care to ensure containment procedures have not been obsoleted.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-136059-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;em&gt;Kinetoglyphs, or kinetohazards, are mental and physical hazards that occur when an entity performs specific gestures and motions that interact with multiple spatial dimensions simultaneously, often with disastrous consequences.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
